# Line-ending policy for a repository edited on Windows and verified on Linux CI.
#
# Without this file the result depends on each machine's core.autocrlf, which is how two
# generated catalogs (config/syllabi/2026-2/NEURO.yaml and config/teaching_logs/2026-2/NEURO.yaml)
# once flipped from CRLF to LF and turned a 25-line change into a 450-line diff.

# Store every text file with LF; check it out with the platform's own endings.
* text=auto

# Calendar exports: iCalendar mandates CRLF (RFC 5545), and scripts/export_calendar_ics.py
# writes it deliberately. Keep that in the working copy on every platform.
*.ics text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Published teaching material Git must never rewrite.
*.pdf binary
*.epub binary
